  "id": "process-evaluation",
  "term": "process evaluation",
  "definition": "Process evaluation is the systematic study of how an intervention is put into practice, including how it is delivered, received, and experienced. It is used alongside outcome evaluation to explain why a program succeeds or fails in real-world settings and to clarify the processes behind its results.",
